    "title": "Endangered Person Advisory issued for 48-year-old man - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Daesha Gear ,\n50 minutes ago\nST. LOUIS COUNTY, Mo. – The St. Louis County Police Department (SLCPD) has issued an Endangered Person Advisory for a man who has been missing since Sept. 10.\nAccording to police, 48-year-old Torey Watson was last seen at 10083 Neville Walk—which is close to Chambers Road—around 8 a.m.\nWatson’s family informed SLCPD that they have not heard from him since Sept. 10 and that he was not taking medication that was prescribed for his mental health diagnoses.\nOfficials say they are unsure if Watson was on foot or in a vehicle at the time of his disappearance.\nThe 48-year-old is described as a Black male who is about 5’9” and weighs 275 pounds. Watson is said to have black hair and brown eyes. In Watson’s missing report, no clothing description was provided.\nAnyone who has seen Torey Watson or has any information about his disappearance is asked to contact 911 to reach their nearest law enforcement agency or contact SLCPD at 636-529-8210.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 2.",
